From ec2ffc2db7b4ef856d774762e051ee1117ffd0d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 03:25:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 369/488] soh: name the 28 address-named symbols defined in
 z_en_heishi2.c

SoH carries the Ocarina of Time decomp, in which several thousand symbols are
still named after their ROM address. This commit names every such symbol DEFINED
IN ONE FILE, so the work can be reviewed a file at a time.

The file names the unit; it does not bound it. Each rename is applied wherever
the symbol occurs -- the declaration in the header, the definition, and every
call site -- so this commit reaches into whatever other files use these symbols
and leaves no dangling reference. It is a pure rename: no behaviour changes, and
the only edits that are not renames are the provenance comments described below.

Two name sources are used, and every name says which it came from:

  * zeldaret/oot -- SoH's decomp IS zeldaret/oot at the same ROM addresses, so
    where oot has already named a symbol, that name is adopted verbatim. The
    definition gets a "Name from zeldaret/oot" comment and every declaration a
    short "// was <addr> [oot]" tag.

  * DEDUCED -- oot leaves a great many symbols address-named too, so those
    names are inferred from the body and its callers, and are marked as OURS
    rather than passed off as upstream. The definition gets
    "LLM generated name (HIGH|GUESS), was <addr>: <reason>" and the short tag
    reads "[LLM:HIGH]" or "[LLM:GUESS]". A GUESS is tagged at every call site
    as well, not only the declaration, so a reader who meets the name anywhere
    knows it is inferred. "git grep '[LLM:'" lists every place the decomp
    leans on an inference.

The justification recorded for each individual name follows, one entry per
symbol, in the order the renames were made. Nothing is summarised away: these
are the per-commit reasons from the unsquashed history, with the boilerplate
that was identical in every one of them hoisted into the text above.

All 28 are defined in soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Heishi2/z_en_heishi2.c; updating their references touches 2 files in total.

  * func_80A531E4 -> EnHeishi2_SetupBribeIdle
    deduced, confidence HIGH: loops gEnHeishiIdleAnim and hands the type 2
    guard to its bribe-text chooser

  * func_80A53278 -> EnHeishi2_ChooseBribeText
    deduced, confidence HIGH: picks the type 2 guard's line from the
    spiritual stones, the time of day, the gate's open flag and whether the
    pocket egg has been obtained

  * func_80A5344C -> EnHeishi2_HandleBribeChoice
    deduced, confidence HIGH: reads the yes/no choice, takes 10 rupees when
    the player can pay, and otherwise refuses

  * func_80A53538 -> EnHeishi2_WaitBribeAccepted
    deduced, confidence HIGH: waits out the paid-up textbox, halts the
    actors and starts the spear slam

  * func_80A535BC -> EnHeishi2_StartSpearSlamFence
    deduced, confidence HIGH: plays gEnHeishiSlamSpearAnim once for the type
    2 guard's fence

  * func_80A53638 -> EnHeishi2_SlamSpearFence
    deduced, confidence HIGH: plays NA_SE_EV_SPEAR_HIT at frame 12 and, at
    the end of the animation, tells the Bg_Spot15_Saku fence to open

  * func_80A5372C -> EnHeishi2_SetupWatchFence
    deduced, confidence HIGH: returns to the idle animation and parks a
    sub-camera on the fence for 200 frames

  * func_80A53850 -> EnHeishi2_WatchFence
    deduced, confidence HIGH: holds the sub-camera until the timer runs out
    or the fence finishes, then restores the main camera and marks the gate
    open

  * func_80A53908 -> EnHeishi2_SetupGateIdle
    deduced, confidence HIGH: loops gEnHeishiIdleAnim and hands the type 5
    guard to its text chooser

  * func_80A5399C -> EnHeishi2_ChooseGateText
    deduced, confidence HIGH: picks the castle-town guard's line from the
    letter flag, the Keaton mask and any face reaction

  * func_80A53AD4 -> EnHeishi2_WaitForZeldasLetter
    deduced, confidence HIGH: offers the letter exchange and chimes when the
    player hands Zelda's letter over

  * func_80A53C0C -> EnHeishi2_WaitLetterTextDone
    deduced, confidence HIGH: waits out the letter textbox, halts the actors
    and starts the spear slam

  * func_80A53C90 -> EnHeishi2_StartSpearSlamGate
    deduced, confidence HIGH: plays gEnHeishiSlamSpearAnim once for the town
    gate

  * func_80A53D0C -> EnHeishi2_SlamSpearGate
    deduced, confidence HIGH: plays NA_SE_EV_SPEAR_HIT at frame 12 and, at
    the end, sets the Bg_Gate_Shutter opening

  * func_80A53DF8 -> EnHeishi2_SetupWatchGate
    deduced, confidence HIGH: returns to the idle animation and parks a
    sub-camera on the town gate for 200 frames

  * func_80A53F30 -> EnHeishi2_WatchGate
    deduced, confidence HIGH: holds the sub-camera until the gate finishes,
    then branches on whether this was the letter, a re-open or the mask
    payout

  * func_80A54038 -> EnHeishi2_FinishLetterText
    deduced, confidence HIGH: sets
    INFTABLE_SHOWED_ZELDAS_LETTER_TO_GATE_GUARD and returns to the gate idle

  * func_80A540C0 -> EnHeishi2_HandleMaskChoice
    deduced, confidence HIGH: reads the sell-the-mask choice, takes the
    Keaton mask and marks it sold, or declines

  * func_80A541FC -> EnHeishi2_WaitMaskSoldText
    deduced, confidence HIGH: waits out the sold text and pays the player 15
    rupees

  * func_80A5427C -> EnHeishi2_WaitPaymentText
    deduced, confidence HIGH: waits out the payment text and either returns
    to idle or slams the spear to work the gate again

  * func_80A54320 -> EnHeishi2_StartSpearSlamCloseGate
    deduced, confidence HIGH: plays gEnHeishiSlamSpearAnim once with the sfx
    flag cleared, for the closing pass

  * func_80A543A0 -> EnHeishi2_SlamSpearCloseGate
    deduced, confidence HIGH: at the end of the slam drives Bg_Gate_Shutter
    to its closing or mask-payout state

  * func_80A544AC -> EnHeishi2_TipOver
    deduced, confidence HIGH: leans the guard's roll to -6100 and opens text
    0x708F once he is down

  * func_80A5455C -> EnHeishi2_DropBomb
    deduced, confidence HIGH: on the text advancing, throws an EN_BOM out at
